    {
      "id": "p0039-b003",
      "kind": "paragraph",
      "source": {
        "text": "Undertale looks at things differently. Instead of hurting enemies, you can talk to them, flatter them, insult them, comfort them, mock them, befriend them, and more, until they lose the will to fight. In short, you can complete the game without killing anything or anyone. Or, if you want, you can slaughter everything you see - the choice is up to you. The game also changes with each choice you make, ensuring that no two Undertale experiences are exactly the same.",
        "raw": "Undertale looks at things differently. Instead of hurting enemies, you can talk\nto them, flatter them, insult them, comfort them, mock them, befriend them,\nand more, until they lose the will to fight. In short, you can complete the game\nwithout killing anything or anyone. Or, if you want, you can slaughter everything\nyou see - the choice is up to you. The game also changes with each choice you\nmake, ensuring that no two Undertale experiences are exactly the same.",
        "status": "corrected",
        "languages": [
          "en"
        ],
        "bbox": [
          0.10582425,
          0.17355714,
          0.70942223,
          0.27717143
        ],
        "mask_bbox": [
          0.10224944,
          0.17284286,
          0.7114362,
          0.27824286
        ],
        "line_ids": [
          8,
          9,
          10,
          11,
          12,
          13
        ]
      },
      "translation": {
        "text": "Undertale 换了个角度。你不必伤害敌人，可以与他们交谈、奉承、辱骂、安慰、嘲弄，或交朋友，直到他们不再想打。你可以不杀任何东西、任何人就通关；也可以随心所欲地杀光眼前的一切，选择在你。游戏还会随每次选择发生变化，没有两段 Undertale 体验会完全一样。",
        "status": "draft",
        "spans": [
